{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_qtcstlzrjuys4l44czx4q7no7otf4mieccsziog2howaik773erq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The project builds successfully with only minor non-functional warnings (one about the crate name in Cargo.toml which I shouldn't modify, and one about an initial value of `b` that gets overwritten in all branches - which is harmless).\n\nSummary of the translation:\n- **`castom_abs`**: Returns absolute value of an i32 using `x > 0 ? x : -x`\n- **`castom_fabs`**: Returns absolute value of f64 with the same logic\n- **`castom_sqrt`**: Newton's method (Babylonian) for square root, returns NaN for negative or NaN input\n- **`castom_floor`/`castom_ceil`/`castom_trunc`**: Integer truncation-based implementations matching the C bounds checks\n- **`castom_fmod`**: `x - trunc(x/y) * y`\n- **`castom_exp`**: Taylor series for exp(x)\n- **`castom_log`**: Logarithm via reduction by powers of e then continued-fraction-like series\n- **`castom_sin`/`castom_cos`**: Taylor series with fmod reduction\n- **`castom_tan`**: Special-cased common values, otherwise sin/cos\n- **`castom_asin`/`castom_acos`/`castom_atan`**: Taylor series for asin, derived for acos and atan\n- **`castom_pow`**: Recursive handling of negative exponents, integer exponent loop, plus exp/log for fractional part\n- **`castom_factorial`**: Iterative multiplication\n\nAll functions match the C source exactly, no `unsafe`, no FFI, no remaining `unimplemented!()`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":385,"cache_read_input_tokens":26557,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":385,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cf414992-4d96-4413-af19-d443b8eb5b1e","uuid":"3a7490a0-5a43-4d7f-8642-f2fb92db2bcc"}
